---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const checklist = [
  {
    site: "Microsoft Skelton Grange",
    ref: "25/06139/FU",
    url: null as string | null,
    urlLabel: null as string | null,
    urlNote: "No lasting case page yet (only Leeds search)",
    power: "Not disclosed",
    notes:
      "Leeds Plans Panel resolution to grant reported April 2026 (Harworth / press). Still listed as proposed until a live Public Access URL is linked.",
  },
  {
    site: "Microsoft Eggborough",
    ref: "Unknown",
    url: null,
    urlLabel: null,
    urlNote: "No live URL yet",
    power: "Not disclosed",
    notes: "No planning reference or megawatt figure recorded in materials reviewed so far.",
  },
  {
    site: "Drax data centre",
    ref: "Screening / full ref TBD",
    url: null,
    urlLabel: null,
    urlNote: "No live URL yet",
    power: "100 MW phase 1 · up to 1,000 MW stated",
    notes:
      "Figures from press and company materials, not yet a live council planning page. Whether a full environmental impact assessment is needed is disputed.",
  },
  {
    site: "Elsham Tech Park",
    ref: "PA/2025/643",
    url: "https://apps.northlincs.gov.uk/application/pa-2025-643",
    urlLabel: "Open portal",
    urlNote: null,
    power: "Up to 1,000 MW for computing equipment (outline)",
    notes:
      "Committee minded to approve Mar 2026, but the portal records no decision issued (checked 2026-07-15); listed as in planning. Farmland including best and most versatile grades.",
  },
  {
    site: "Humber Tech Park",
    ref: "PA/2024/584",
    url: "https://apps.northlincs.gov.uk/application/pa-2024-584",
    urlLabel: "Open portal",
    urlNote: null,
    power: "386 MW (stated / reporting)",
    notes: "Outline permission Aug 2024 (North Lincs). Acreage still to confirm against drawings.",
  },
  {
    site: "Deep Green Bradford",
    ref: "Unknown",
    url: null,
    urlLabel: null,
    urlNote: "No live URL yet",
    power: "5.6 MW stated",
    notes:
      "Bradford approval reported May 2026 (operator / BBC). Still listed as proposed until a live portal URL is linked.",
  },
];

const leedsLetter = `[Your name]
[Date]

Information Governance
Leeds City Council
[published FOI / EIR email or portal]

Dear Sir/Madam,

Freedom of Information Act 2000 / Environmental Information Regulations 2004

I request information about planning application 25/06139/FU (Microsoft / Skelton Grange data centre, Stourton).

Please provide:

1. The lasting public web address (or the council’s internal case ID) that opens this application’s live page on the Public Access planning system, not only the generic search form.

2. The decision notice, committee report, and any officer report recommending grant or resolution-to-grant, with document titles and dates.

3. Any Environmental Statement chapters, energy statements, or utilities/infrastructure notes that state megawatt capacity, grid connection size, water demand, or cooling method for this development (or confirmation that no such figures appear in the application documents held).

4. If any item is already published, please give the direct document URL on Public Access rather than attaching duplicates.

I am happy to receive the response electronically. If the cost limit applies, please advise how to refine the request. This is for a public-interest project assembling sourced environmental figures for regional data centre proposals (The Yorkshire Compute Belt).

Yours faithfully,
[Name]
[Email]`;

const waterLetter = `[Your name]
[Date]

Information Governance / EIR
Yorkshire Water
[published EIR address]

Dear Sir/Madam,

Environmental Information Regulations 2004: request for information

I am requesting environmental information about water supply and wastewater impacts of proposed and consented data centre developments in Yorkshire and the Humber.

Please treat this as a request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.

For the period 1 January 2020 to the date of your response, please provide:

1. Any assessments, capacity studies, network constraint notes, or correspondence assessing the impact on public water supply or sewerage/wastewater capacity of data centre or “tech park” developments at or near:
   a) Skelton Grange / Stourton, Leeds (also referred to as Microsoft Skelton Grange);
   b) Eggborough, North Yorkshire (Microsoft);
   c) Drax Power Station site, Selby / North Yorkshire (data centre proposals);
   d) Elsham Tech Park, North Lincolnshire (planning ref PA/2025/643);
   e) Humber Tech Park, North Lincolnshire (planning ref PA/2024/584);
   f) Land east of Bradford Energy Centre / Listerhills, Bradford (Deep Green / heat-reuse data centre).

2. For each of the above where held: stated or estimated annual or peak water demand (megalitres or litres), whether supply is potable / non-potable / private, and any discharge consent volumes or temperatures relevant to cooling or process water.

3. Any documents in which an operator or applicant claimed “zero water use”, “eliminates water usage”, or closed-loop / no potable offtake for a data centre in your area, and Yorkshire Water’s recorded view on that claim (agreement, caveat, or rejection).

4. If information is held but some sites have none, please say so site by site rather than refusing the whole request.

I am happy to receive information electronically. If any part exceeds the cost limit or engages an exception, please advise what can be disclosed within the limit and how I might refine the request.

This information is sought for a public-interest project assembling sourced environmental figures for data centre proposals in the region (The Yorkshire Compute Belt). I do not seek personal data of individuals.

Yours faithfully,
[Name]
[Email]`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="Verification gaps and sample information-request letters for documenting the physical footprint of data centres across Yorkshire and the Humber."
>
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl m-0 tracking-tight">Research</h1>
  <p class="text-[var(--muted)] mt-2 max-w-2xl">
    Closing these gaps is how the map gets closer to the real physical footprint: power, land, water, and
    live planning evidence. Figures stay provisional until the items below are filled.
    How we use evidence is on <a href={`${base}/methodology`}>Methodology</a>.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-12" id="hard-rule">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl m-0">Our rule on status</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      No status above <strong>proposed</strong> without a link that opens the live planning application
      (not a search form).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" id="checklist">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl m-0">Site checklist</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-[var(--ink)] text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--muted)]">
            <th class="py-2 pr-3">Site</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-3">Planning ref</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-3">Live URL</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-3">Stated size</th>
            <th class="py-2">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {checklist.map((row) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--line)] align-top">
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-3 font-medium">{row.site}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-3 font-tabular">{row.ref}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-3">
                {row.url ? (
                  <a href={row.url} rel="noopener">{row.urlLabel ?? "Open portal"}</a>
                ) : (
                  <span class="text-[var(--muted)]">{row.urlNote}</span>
                )}
              </td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-3">{row.power}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 text-[var(--muted)]">{row.notes}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" id="outstanding">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl m-0">Outstanding before we treat figures as fully checked</h2>
    <ol class="mt-3 max-w-2xl space-y-2">
      <li>Save an archived copy of every source link when we add it.</li>
      <li>Find lasting council planning pages for Skelton, Deep Green, Drax, and Eggborough, then update statuses where that allows.</li>
      <li>Cite exact pages inside planning PDFs, not only committee-report summaries.</li>
      <li>Check map pins against the official site-boundary drawings in each application.</li>
      <li>Confirm Humber acreage and megawatts against PA/2024/584 documents, not press alone.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" id="local-consumption">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl m-0">Local consumption</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      Local-authority electricity totals loaded from Department for Energy Security and Net Zero
      subnational statistics (2024 rows) on 2026-07-15.
      Download: <a href={`${base}/data/local_consumption.json`}>local consumption figures</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" id="foi">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl m-0">Sample information-request letters</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">
      These are templates you can copy. Prefer the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 for environmental
      holdings (water, emissions, planning environment material). Prefer the Freedom of Information Act 2000
      for other council records. Send one public authority at a time via their published channel.
    </p>

    <h3 class="font-display text-lg m-0 mt-8" id="foi-leeds">Leeds City Council · Skelton Grange</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)] mt-2 max-w-2xl">
      Goal: a lasting link to the live planning case page for application 25/06139/FU, plus any power, water, or cooling figures on file.
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 max-w-3xl overflow-x-auto text-xs leading-relaxed bg-white/50 border border-[var(--line)] p-4 whitespace-pre-wrap font-mono text-[var(--ink)]">{leedsLetter}</pre>

    <h3 class="font-display text-lg m-0 mt-10" id="foi-yorkshire-water">Yorkshire Water · water capacity and zero-water claims</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)] mt-2 max-w-2xl">
      Target: offtake, discharge, and whether “zero water” claims have been recorded or challenged.
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-3 max-w-3xl overflow-x-auto text-xs leading-relaxed bg-white/50 border border-[var(--line)] p-4 whitespace-pre-wrap font-mono text-[var(--ink)]">{waterLetter}</pre>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
